--- !u!114 &-4867663930508900321
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "<b>Volumes</b> allow you to override certain settings per Camera, such as post-processing effects. These property overrides are stored in assets on disk called <b>Volume Profiles.</b>\n\nThere are two main types of Volumes: <b>Global</b> and <b>Local.</b>\n\n\u2022 A <b>Global Volume</b> lives inside the Scene as a Volume GameObject component. It can be considered infinitely large and is useful to control properties affecting the entire world.\n\n\u2022 A <b>Local Volume</b> also lives inside the Scene as a Volume GameObject component; however, it is used to override Volume properties within a very specific area of the scene via a Box, Sphere, Capsule or Mesh collider."
--- !u!114 &-4465089028539258207
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: 'In this tutorial, you learned how Global and Local Volumes can be used to override the URP effects based on the camera position.


      For more details, check out the corresponding <a href="https://docs.unity3d.com/Packages/com.unity.render-pipelines.universal@latest/index.html?subfolder=/manual/Volumes.html">documentation.</a>


      <b>Note:</b> You do not need to save your changes in order to follow other tutorials.'
